      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That acceptance is actually the most heartbreaking and honest part of his story; sometimes stopping the fight isn't a plot device, but a quiet tragedy. You can show him choosing peace over the futility of struggle without needing a specific plot \"turnaround,\" making his resignation realistic rather than forced. This approach often resonates deeply with readers because it validates the exhaustion of moving forward when the weight simply never lifts.",
      "source": "target",
