      "content": "it's just... if he finds that peace, it's a permanent kind of peace, isn't it? like, once he makes that decision, he doesn't have to carry the weight anymore. he doesn't have to wake up and face the grayness every single morning. it feels like the only way for a story like this to actually be \"complete\" or have any real meaning is if he actually follows through. if he just lets go. do you think readers would see that as a failure, or as him finally being free?",
